                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I recently received this game for free as a curator connect offer for my group Visual novel, JRPG, Anime. First of all, this visual novel is an adult eroge visual novel with a few NSFW CGs. For those who don't mind adult visual novels, read on.\n\nThis romance visual novel with arcade racing and platforming segments by Dev9k features a male protagonist Mitur Aldaine. Mitur graduated from an Academy and became the greatest racer of Alba Proxima and an Eye in a futuristic world where territorial contests between different orbital stations are decided by races among spaceships.\n\nAs an Eye, Mitur is tasked with providing guidance and directions to pilots involved in flying spaceships in such races remotely from an orbital station and having a compatible Nirvana Synchronicity. However, a sudden lack of focus due to a conflicting set of emotions he felt for two different women in his life caused the death of a pilot and Mitur to be disgraced and retire from professional racing where a rival orbital station Merols seized and took over a rich cobalt district in Mars as a result of Mitur's loss in the race.\n\n10 years later, Mitur receives a visit by Apprentice Pilot Yume Kichi Neleiad. Yume brought her own spaceship with an insistent request for Mitur to be her Eye and take up racing again. Mitur becomes Yume's Eye and guides her across 10 different racing tracks on a path of redemption to make amends for the loss in the race 10 years earlier. Mitur will allow a female journalist Eleanor Esch to hang around him to do her exclusive biography special on Mitur, calling a close female friend who is an Upekkha scientist Mai Paget for help in fixing a problem with the spaceship and also have unpleasant encounters with an antagonist Anselm Jagasit. This may lead to a romance scene or ending with Mai, Eleanor or Yume.\n\nAfter playing this game for around 3 hours to read through the storyline, complete all race tracks and get all achievements, the game has surprisingly good backstory as a futuristic science fiction visual novel. This could potentially have opportunities for additional side-stories or sequels by being interesting in highlighting the rivalry between two orbital stations and the protagonist's differences with the Academy and Senate in Alba Proxima. The game also has nice synthwave music by Retröxx which are appropriate for the futuristic science fiction themes and 80's TV sets featured in this visual novel where my favourite BGM is Retröspect (Reprise) which is played at the title screen and just before the final racing track for its stirring and uplifting music. For those who have difficulty playing through the arcade racing/platforming segments to reach the best ending in the game, the game has an arcade mode which allows players to choose any racing track to play on without using progress from the game's story mode.\n\nAmong the cons, the game as a romance visual novel feels rushed by not adequately covering the relationship between the protagonist and each main character well. As an arcade racer and platformer, it also has a few bugs where the spaceship may crash out and restart level occasionally when passing through a transition point along the racing track, there was also one instance where the screen keeps flashing white every few seconds until the level is restarted.\n\nOverall, this game is recommended when at discount or bundle offer for those who like a short romance visual novel with nice background music, decent anime artwork, arcade racing/platforming elements, easy achievements and like or don't mind a few adult CGs in the game.\n\n[h1]Visual novel, JRPG, Anime Steam group - Join the group and consider following the group's curator list for more reviews or recommended romance visual novels with at least one good ending[/h1]\n\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/groups/vnislife\n\n[h1]Achievements events group - Join the group and consider following the group's curator list for more reviews or games with easy/reasonable achievements[/h1]\n\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/groups/GroupAchievements100",
